   "grading": "Pass requires sub-tests (a) and (b) to pass, with the procurement package and license terms explicit at bid time; where the interface is not self-descriptive at runtime, sub-test (c) is also required, and an integration manual that is absent or available only for an extra fee is then a Fail, because the interface cannot be integrated without it. Where the interface is self-descriptive, sub-test (c) is a SHOULD: a paywalled or missing manual is recorded as a gap but does not by itself Fail C4. Partial is reserved for cases in which ambiguous clauses exist but the vendor provides a written contract amendment before purchase. A clause is ambiguous within the meaning of this criterion only when its scope is genuinely unclear and the restriction, if the clause were interpreted most broadly, would not independently qualify as a Fail condition. A clause that, under any plausible interpretation, imposes one or more Fail conditions — field-of-use restriction on buyer-written integration code, per-deployment royalties, or restriction to vendor-approved integrations — is Fail regardless of a vendor's offered amendment, unless the amendment fully removes the clause rather than merely clarifying its scope. Fail covers any of: API access unavailable for the intended workflow, gating after purchase, restriction to vendor-approved integrations, per-deployment royalties, or prohibition on publication or reuse of integration code.",
