     "t": "When the control session is lost, meaning the control client stops sending heartbeats or commands for a configurable interval, the instrument MUST make that loss observable: it detects the timeout and exposes a control-session-lost status through the normal status channel, so that the orchestrator or a middle-layer controller can decide on and drive the appropriate response.",
